WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.567
CI/CD for models.

2
00:00:02.867 --> 00:00:05.021
New data, same code, worse model.

3
00:00:05.021 --> 00:00:07.633
So the pipeline has to gate on evidence.

4
00:00:08.833 --> 00:00:13.567
CI/CD for models is software delivery discipline, with one twist.

5
00:00:13.867 --> 00:00:17.700
Datasets and metrics become first-class citizens of the pipeline.

6
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:23.267
The eval suite plays the role of unit tests: an executable definition of still works.

7
00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:25.733
Here is the pipeline.

8
00:00:26.033 --> 00:00:27.500
A pull request arrives.

9
00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:31.067
We validate the data: schema, ranges, and nulls.

10
00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:33.800
We retrain and run the evaluation suite.

11
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.433
The gate checks the metric against a threshold.

12
00:00:36.733 --> 00:00:38.633
Only if it passes do we release.

13
00:00:39.833 --> 00:00:41.400
Three pieces make this work.

14
00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:46.766
Continuous integration: every pull request runs data validation and eval.

15
00:00:46.766 --> 00:00:51.000
A metric below the threshold is a red X, like a failing test.

16
00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:57.833
Continuous delivery: merged changes reach staging automatically, and production goes through the registry.

17
00:00:58.133 --> 00:01:04.667
And continuous training: a drift alarm or a schedule can trigger the pipeline with no human pull request.

18
00:01:05.867 --> 00:01:07.333
Here is a minimal gate.

19
00:01:07.633 --> 00:01:09.533
It runs on every pull request.

20
00:01:09.833 --> 00:01:13.100
One step runs the evaluation and writes the metrics.

21
00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:19.233
The next reads them, and fails with a red X if the AUC falls below zero point nine one.

22
00:01:20.433 --> 00:01:21.788
Here is a real catch.

23
00:01:21.788 --> 00:01:25.850
A teammate swaps the embedding model of a RAG system for speed.

24
00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:27.333
Code review looks fine.

25
00:01:27.633 --> 00:01:34.800
But CI runs the evaluation suite, and faithfulness drops from zero point eight eight to zero point seven nine.

26
00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:38.889
Red X, merge blocked, with the metric diff in the check output.

27
00:01:38.889 --> 00:01:40.633
The pipeline is the noticing.

28
00:01:41.833 --> 00:01:42.607
Let's recap.

29
00:01:42.607 --> 00:01:44.733
Models can break from data alone.

30
00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:47.133
Eval suites are the new unit tests.

31
00:01:47.433 --> 00:01:50.333
CI gates, CD ships, and CT retrains.

32
00:01:50.633 --> 00:01:52.238
Evidence, or no deploy.

33
00:01:52.238 --> 00:01:53.633
Next up: monitoring.
